From 34d7e73fdafb0e8fcb2e1e71bb19f2515740a773 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AOSP RK3576 Baseline <uhf-platform@localbuild>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 09:46:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] uhf: switch UhfService to the Phase 2 HAL transport,
 retire the JNI path
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Completes the swap the Phase 1 commit messages promised UhfTransport was
designed for:

- UhfHalTransport (new): a thin Binder proxy to rockchip.uhf.aidl.IUhfReader
  (see the hardware/rockchip/uhf commit alongside this one). Resolves the
  HAL lazily via ServiceManager.waitForDeclaredService, links to its death
  (NFR-R-01), and drops the cached proxy on death so the next call
  re-resolves it rather than UhfHalTransport itself attempting any restart
  logic — init already owns that via the HAL class hal service entry.

- UhfSerialTransport.java and its JNI .cpp are deleted, not deprecated —
  SRS §10.2 Phase 2 lists "JNI path removed" as an explicit exit
  criterion, and UhfSessionArbiter needing zero changes across this swap
  (still 74/74 tests passing, unmodified) is the actual proof that
  UhfTransport was the right seam.

- UhfService.getReaders(): the diagnostic "device path" field now reports
  the HAL instance string rather than a tty path system_server no longer
  even knows — Phase 2 deliberately moves that knowledge into the vendor
  process.

- UhfService.BinderStreamCallback.onTagBatch(): closes a real gap left in
  Phase 1 rather than carrying it forward. Streamed tag records now go
  through UhfProtocol.decodeTagRecords (the same decode inventory() uses)
  instead of being wrapped as placeholder UhfTag objects with zeroed
  EPC/RSSI — the HAL callback already hands over one complete record per
  array element, so no concatenation is needed first.

74/74 UhfProtocol/UhfSessionArbiter tests still pass, unmodified — neither
class imports anything about Binder, AIDL, or a specific transport
implementation, which is the whole reason this swap did not touch them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
