-// Backs com.android.server.uhf.UhfSerialTransport's native methods: open/configure/read/write/
-// close/purge on the reader's tty, per UHF-SRS-001 FR-LNK-01/08.
-//
-// STATUS: written, not built or run. This has not been compiled (would need this file registered
-// in services/core/jni/onload.cpp and a services.core Android.bp native lib target, neither of
-// which this patch touches — deliberately, since getting that registration wrong risks the many
-// other HALs already wired through the same onload.cpp), and there is no reader attached to this
-// environment to exercise it against even if it were built. It is standard termios usage with no
-// UHF-specific logic in it at all — every byte it hands to Java goes through UhfProtocol's already
-// -tested parser before anything trusts it — but "standard" is not "verified"; treat this file the
-// same way the SRS's own Confirm status treats an inferred command code.
-//
-// One value genuinely is unconfirmed rather than merely untested: FR-LNK-01 specifies 115200 8N1,
-// which this hardcodes via kBaudRate/cfmakeraw's defaults (8 data bits, no parity, one stop bit,
